<title>JAPAN: Aseed says to buy back 154,000 shares.</title>
<headline>Aseed says to buy back 154,000 shares.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Aseed Co Ltd, a retailer specialising in drinks and food for vending machines, said on Tuesday that it would buy back 154,000 of its shares worth 300 million yen in order to introduce a stock-option scheme.  </p>
<p>The scheme needs to be approved by a shareholders' meeting on June 27.</p>
<p>The stock options will be offered to eight directors and 42 higher-ranked employees.</p>
<p>The exercise period starts on July 1, 1998, and ends on March 31, 2003.</p>
</text>
